# Full scraped article text never leaves the machine (D14, §1.3(2)).
# The corpus INDEX is public-safe and is committed; the article bodies are not.
*/corpus/articles/
*/corpus/versions/*/articles/
# What `newsab_corpus fetch` writes: whole publisher pages as served, including the
# `*.refused.html` a both-layer refusal is judged from.  Same rule, one step earlier.
*/corpus/raw/
# Everything staged is article text — ignore the whole directory rather than a list of
# suffixes, so a quarantined file (e.g. `*.yaml.excluded`) cannot leak by not matching.
*/corpus/staging/*
!*/corpus/staging/EXAMPLE.yaml.template
*/gold/worksheet.json
